+# Derived Pure-Result Persistence Plan
+
+Status: implemented
+Governing contract: `specs/state.md` (Result Persistence Profile)
+
+## Goal
+
+Compiler-generated `pure_projection` steps are deterministic functions of earlier
+durable results and bound inputs. Under `result_persistence_profile:
+derived_pure_replay.v1` an eligible step persists only a value-free completion
+shell and resume re-derives its values in memory.
+
+## Approach
+
+One owner for the profile: `orchestrator/workflow/pure_result_replay.py` (a facade
+over `pure_replay_core` shell/progress, `pure_replay_index` eligibility and
+`pure_replay_runtime` replay). State, outcome recorder, executor, lexical
+checkpoints and default resume only consult it.
+
+## Harder later
+
+A second derivable step kind needs its own eligibility rule in the index. The
+overlay is a second value source; readers go through `PureReplayRuntime`.
+
+## Verification
+
+`tests/test_state_result_persistence_profile.py`, `tests/test_call_frame_state_profile.py`,
+`tests/test_pure_result_replay_index.py`, `tests/test_pure_replay_progress.py`,
+`tests/test_pure_replay_resume.py` (end-to-end crash/resume through the CLI).
