--- a/specs/state.md
+++ b/specs/state.md
@@ -577,6 +577,71 @@
   Root/callee checksums, lexical checkpoint validation, and
   projection-integrity guards remain unchanged.
 
+## Result Persistence Profile (`result_persistence_profile`)
+
+`state.json` may carry an optional top-level `result_persistence_profile`. Absent
+means the historical bundle-backed persistence: `to_dict()` omits the key,
+`from_dict()` of a payload without it yields `None`, and the payload round-trips
+unchanged. The only supported present value is `derived_pure_replay.v1`; any
+other value fails closed with a `ValueError` naming the profile at `RunState`
+construction, at `StateManager.initialize(...)`, and on load (a failed load never
+rewrites the file). `schema_version` stays `2.1`; the field is additive.
+
+- Selection
+  - `StateManager.initialize(..., result_persistence_profile=None)` writes the
+    field in the single initial atomic write, before any visit. Generic callers
+    stay explicit opt-in; loads never infer, backfill or upgrade it.
+  - A successfully compiled typed public `.orc` run (`orchestrator run`) and a
+    new root created by `orchestrator resume --force-restart` select the
+    profile. The force-restart source run is only read.
+  - A fresh non-iterative child call frame whose callee bundle has the validated
+    provenance `frontend_kind == "workflow_lisp"` selects it, including a fresh
+    retry after a failed non-iterative predecessor (the predecessor frame stays
+    unchanged). Existing frames, non-Workflow-Lisp callees and iteration-owned
+    child frames keep the historical profile; an existing frame is never
+    backfilled. A malformed existing frame (no `state`, or a non-mapping `state`)
+    is rejected with `ValueError("malformed existing call-frame state ...")`
+    before anything is written. `load_existing_call_frame_read_only(frame)` returns
+    a detached copy of that state without writes.
+- Eligibility. A compiler-generated `pure_projection` that is acyclic and visited
+  at most once per scope is eligible. Recurrent, loop-owned and other multiply
+  visited pure nodes (`multiple_visit_region`) keep full durable rows, bundles and
+  checkpoints even inside a profiled root. Refs are scoped to the workflow that
+  holds them; an imported callee bundle is indexed under its own scope `root`.
+  `derive_pure_result_replay_index` is the single authority.
+- Completion shell. A successful eligible pure step persists exactly
+  `{"name", "step_id", "visit_count": 1, "status": "completed", "exit_code": 0,
+  "outcome": {"status": "completed", "phase": "execution", "class": "completed",
+  "retryable": false}, "result_storage": "derived_pure_replay.v1"}` and nothing
+  else (no value, output, text, json, artifacts, debug, duration or bundle).
+  Failed and skipped rows stay full durable rows. No private lineage
+  (`private_artifact_versions`), pure result bundle or checkpoint record is written
+  for an eligible node, and `workflow_outputs` are unchanged.
+- Visit atomicity. `begin_eligible_pure_visit` increments the visit and publishes
+  the running cursor in one write; `settle_eligible_pure_success` / `_failure`
+  persist the row and clear the cursor in one write. Progress is classified as
+  `unstarted`, `interrupted`, `derived_complete` or `durable_failure_skip`;
+  every other combination is `progress_witness_invalid`.
+- Resume. Values are re-derived in memory (never dispatching an effect,
+  incrementing a visit, settling a result or writing state) from bound inputs and
+  durable rows. A resume fails closed before any effect with
+  `error.type == "pure_result_replay_unavailable"` and `error.context.reason` one
+  of `durable_input_missing`, `durable_input_invalid`, `binding_unresolved`,
+  `evaluation_failed`, `output_contract_invalid`, `progress_witness_invalid`,
+  `dependency_index_invalid`, `reachability_ambiguous` or `profile_conflict`.
+  A persisted value row, pure bundle or private-lineage entry for an eligible node
+  (`context.surface` of `steps`, `pure_bundle`, `private_artifact_versions`), or
+  an eligible node's checkpoint record or restore binding in the same scope
+  (`checkpoint_record`, `restore_payload`), is a `profile_conflict`.
+- Default resume. Replay-eligible pure points are filtered out of the checkpoint
+  candidates before unique-nearest selection and emit no record. The only
+  zero-record admission is `VALIDATED_FRAME_ENTRY_REPLAY`
+  (`selection_reason: validated_frame_entry_replay`, `checkpoint_id: null`); it
+  needs validated bound-input leaves, exact profile and progress witnesses and a
+  durable owner, otherwise it fails closed with
+  `lexical_default_resume_prior_boundary_not_restorable`. A restorable nearest
+  non-eligible point keeps `validated_prior_boundary`.
+
 ## Reusable-Call State Contract (v2.5)
 
 - Caller-visible exports
